   "daf": "67a",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "עַל כׇּל סוּכָּה וְסוּכָּה אוֹמְרִים לוֹ: הֲרֵי מָזוֹן וַהֲרֵי מַיִם. תָּנָא: מֵעוֹלָם לֹא הוּצְרַךְ אָדָם לְכָךְ, אֶלָּא שֶׁאֵינוֹ דּוֹמֶה מִי שֶׁיֵּשׁ לוֹ פַּת בְּסַלּוֹ, לְמִי שֶׁאֵין לוֹ פַּת בְּסַלּוֹ.",
   "en": "It was taught in the mishna: «At each and every booth» people there «say to him: Here is food; here is water,» if you need it. It was «taught: No man» who escorted the goat «ever needed this» food and water. «However,» they would offer it to him anyway, «because one who has bread in his basket is not similar to one who does not have bread in his basket.» One who does not have food available to him is concerned that he will not be able to find any if he really needs it, and he therefore feels his hunger and thirst more acutely."
  }
 ],
